  "title": "AI coding guardrails are mostly the old guardrails",
  "summary": "The tools are new. The pace of development can be faster. The actual safety controls are, for the most part, the same unglamorous ones backend teams have relied on for years. We have not discovered a new law of physics. We have mostly rediscovered the old ones with an LLM-powered coding agent attached.",
